  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3 Technologies has recorded $418M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The company received 252 awards so far and the average award size is $1.7M. Obligations are down 26.8% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $350M, followed by the General Services Administration with $62.9M and the Department of Homeland Security with $4.6M. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market with $123M in obligations, followed by Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) at $118M and Engineering Services at $65.9M. Fiscal-year obligations show variability: FY21 totaled $466M, FY22 totaled $227M, FY23 totaled $451M, FY24 totaled $613M, FY25 totaled $570M, and FY26 is $418M to date. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has L3 Technologies' federal contracting trended year over year?",
        "body": "L3 Technologies' FY2026 obligations are $418M. Obligations fell 26.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $466M in FY21, $227M in FY22, $451M in FY23, $613M in FY24, and $570M in FY25. The current FY26 total is a fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets does L3 Technologies serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $350M, the General Services Administration obligated $62.9M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $4.6M in FY2026 to date. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $123M, Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) accounted for $118M, and Engineering Services accounted for $65.9M. Other notable markets include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $65.6M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $7.9M. The company has 252 awards so far and an average award size of $1.7M."
      }
    ]
